ework  code bases to be accepted  later saw two intel's distributed ledger  was incubated  now let's move to the goals of  hyperledger  first is to facilitate commercial  transaction  create enterprise grade open source  distributed ledger  frameworks and code bases  second is to provide infrastructure that  is impartial  open and community driven with technical  and corporate  governance third is to develop  blockchain  and shared ledger pocs application cases  field trails and deployments build  technical communities  fourth is to educate the general  audience on the blockchain's  technology's  market potential fifth is  to promote our community of communities  by utilizing a toolkit approach  that includes a variety of platforms and  framework  now let's understand the technology  layer of hyperledger  hyperledger employs the following  essential business components in its  architecture  first is the consensus layer it is in  charge of reaching an agreement  on the order and verifying the accuracy  of the blog's transactions  then comes the smart contract layer  which is in charge of processing  transaction requests  and only authorizing transactions that  are valid  after that is the communication layer  peer-to-peer message  transit is handled by the communication  layer  then comes identity management services  these are required for maintaining and  validating user  and system identities as well as  creating trust on the blockchain  and at the end comes the api or  application programming interface  external programs and clients can  interact with the blockchain using the  api  now let's have a look at the  organizational architecture  of hyperledger essentially hyperledger  enables the development of various  blockchain-based systems  and applications for industrial use by  providing the necessary infrastructure  and standards it acts more like a hub  bringing together numerous blockchain  based projects  and tools that follow established design  philosophy  hyperledger's architecture can be  broadly divided into three main  components  which is apis sdks  and clis apis or application programming  interface  include membership services which is a  set of cryptographic certificates  that defines the organization by itself  every pair or order needs this type of  certificate  which consists of some common properties  that signifies  that whether the peer or the order  belongs to the same organization  a pair which is a part of the same  membership services can communicate with  each other but peers from other  organizations cannot communicate with  each other  sdks or software development kits  include  blockchain and transaction layer which  constitutes the core code of the  blockchain  it consists of the consensus algorithm  which helps to make the final decision  on the validation of every transaction  it also consists of distributed ledger  as well as legit storage  which contains all details regarding the  transactions  made 1 and also lastly known status of  each transaction  it has a peer-to-peer protocol used to  communicate between the nodes  on the network clies a command line  interface consists of chain code which  is a layer of logical programming  which consists of the business logic  required to run  in operation on the hyperledger now that  we know all about hyperledger structure  and goals let's understand how  hyperledger works  let's take an example of two friends  alex and sarah  who wants to perform a hyperledger  transaction  sarah runs a bakery and wants to send a  birthday cake to alex  as per his request on the sarah's bakery  app now sarah looks for his address  on her application which sends a query  to the membership services of the  application and validates transaction of  only  directly affiliated peers to the  application  now our application searches for alex's  membership on the membership services  of that particular application for  validation  now after that hyperledger connects both 